{"chunk_id": "8aa1c9dedce2", "text": "This chapter recounts the origins of Ravana and his siblings, set against the earlier defeat of the Rakshasas by Vishnu. After the Rakshasas flee Lanka and dwell in the nether regions under Sumali, the demon king seeks a strategy to restore their power. Seeing Kubera, the radiant son of the sage Vishravas, Sumali resolves that his daughter Kaikasi should bear children by the same sage. Though Vishravas warns that approaching him at an inauspicious hour will produce fierce and evil offspring, Kaikasi persists. She gives birth to the terrible ten\u2011headed Dashagriva (later Ravana), the giant Kumbhakarna, the demoness Shurpanakha, and finally the virtuous Vibhishana. Ominous portents accompany Ravana\u2019s birth, while auspicious signs mark Vibhishana\u2019s. Stirred by his mother\u2019s comparison with Kubera, Dashagriva vows to surpass his brother and begins severe austerities to gain invincible power.\nSumali sends Kaikasi to marry sage Vishravas, leading to the births of Ravana, Kumbhakarna, Shurpanakha, and virtuous Vibhishana.\nThemes: origins of Ravana, fate and omens, ascetic power, family ambition, good vs evil siblings", "vector": [0.018785614520311356, -0.02653198316693306, 0.018461724743247032, -0.0006304888520389795, -0.01695023849606514, 0.015425257384777069, -0.019015036523342133, -0.0204185601323843, -0.024264752864837646, -0.029743891209363937, 0.007881321012973785, 0.00955475214868784, 0.011315903626382351, 0.02346852421760559, -0.011707271449267864, 0.011336146853864193, 0.038030073046684265, -0.03452126681804657, 0.03484515845775604, -0.023239102214574814, -0.002427487401291728, 0.002705830382183194, -0.010371224954724312, -0.002832349855452776, -0.034683212637901306, 0.008873234502971172, 0.016302458941936493, -0.030040789395570755, 0.01597856916487217, -0.009574995376169682, -0.023711441084742546, -0.0013191766338422894, 0.027517147362232208, -0.002694021910429001, -0.029986808076500893, 0.0040486240759491